            <ArticleTitle>Effect of cimetidine on herpes zoster infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>803-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cimetidine was administered to two patients for herpes zoster infection. An acute pain-relieving effect was observed. The patients were followed for 11 and 14 months without developing postherpetic neuralgia. Possible mechanisms for prevention of postherpetic neuralgia by cimetidine are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
